//
// BBS's BaseFilmController.render() loops every replay serially and runs the
// full renderEntity prework (matrix build + 2× world.getLightLevel chunk
// lookup + new FormRenderingContext + FormUtilsClient.render descent down to
// the cancelled render3D). Measured ~7-13ms/frame at ~2900 replays — the FPS
// wall after the bake removed the animator cost.
//
// This bypass replaces that loop for a PURE crowd of "simple" replays:
//   - compute each replay's worldMatrix IN PARALLEL via BBS's own
//     getMatrixForRenderWithRotation (verified bit-exact vs the real captured
//     matrix: bypass-compare logged maxDelta=0 over 8M samples), and
//   - submit straight into FastPathBatch (Tier 2-h draws it at AFTER_ENTITIES).
//   - then cancel the original render() loop entirely.
// Parallel is SAFE here because the bake removed per-frame animation: this loop
// is pure matrix math reading per-replay state, no shared mutable model.
//
// ALL-OR-NOTHING per frame: if ANY replay is not simple-eligible (actor,
// grouped, anchored→relative, non-ModelForm, non-cubic), we do NOT cancel —
// BBS renders the whole frame normally (current behaviour). So mixed/cinematic
// scenes are untouched; only uniform armies take the fast path.
//
// Default OFF (ENABLE_RENDER_LOOP_BYPASS). Opt-in + toggleable → cannot break
// the default experience; verify visually before relying on it.
